WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.182
This query creates January, February, and March admission counts plus a total.

00:00:05.182 --> 00:00:08.482
The left join preserves patients with no admissions.

00:00:08.482 --> 00:00:12.697
Run the query and compare total admissions with the displayed month columns.

00:00:12.697 --> 00:00:17.627
If the dataset contains only those months, the totals should align with their sum.

00:00:17.627 --> 00:00:23.217
Connect this idea to a BI dashboard turning monthly categories into presentation columns.

00:00:23.217 --> 00:00:28.447
Ask what could go wrong if the concept were misunderstood: could rows be duplicated,

00:00:28.447 --> 00:00:35.282
important records disappear, categories be interpreted incorrectly, or a report become difficult to reproduce?

00:00:35.282 --> 00:00:40.477
A strong analyst can explain both the SQL operation and the assumption behind it.

00:00:40.477 --> 00:00:45.680
After the example, summarize the idea in one plain-language sentence before moving on.
